counterfactuals.output:
A method of configuring a graphical user interface for control of a process plant, the method comprising:

displaying, on a display device, a plurality of graphical control objects including a first monitor block, a second monitor block, and an effect block;

receiving, via the graphical user interface, a first user input defining a first connection from an output of the first monitor block to an input of the second monitor block;

receiving, via the graphical user interface, a second user input defining a second connection from an output of the first monitor block to an input of the effect block;

receiving, via the graphical user interface, a third user input defining a third connection from an output of the second monitor block to an input of the effect block; and

receiving, via the graphical user interface, a further user input designating one or more cells associated with at least one of the first monitor block, the second monitor block, or the effect block as trigger cells,

wherein the graphical user interface is configured to represent a control relationship in which data monitored by the first monitor block is provided to the second monitor block and to the effect block, data monitored by the second monitor block is provided to the effect block, and the designated trigger cells define conditions for initiating an effect associated with the effect block.
